infiltrator-calc (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add Programmer mode with binary, octal, decimal and hexadecimal bases.
  * Add 8, 16, 32 and 64-bit integer widths with unsigned/signed display.
  * Add integer bitwise, shift, arithmetic and complement operations.
  * Replace the two-state mode toggle with Standard, Scientific and Programmer modes.
  * Add Programmer-mode regression tests and keep the shared Common-based core architecture.

 -- Shannon Smith <infiltratr@yandex.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +1000

infiltrator-calc (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add reusable calculation variables with name=expression assignment.
  * Add a shared calculation-session layer for variables, memory and bounded history.
  * Add a desktop calculation-history window with clear-history support.
  * Add regression coverage for variable evaluation, session memory and history retention.
  * Keep the existing Standard and Scientific calculator behaviour intact.

